# Blocking jobs return a result snapshot

`startConcatenation` → `waitWithProgress` → read getters → `reset` is easy to get wrong (stale `outputPath_`, empty cancel text, starting while `Running`). Prefer one call that returns a value type.

`VideoConcatenationResult` holds `succeeded`, `outputPath`, `errorMessage`. `runWithProgress` starts, waits, copies those fields, then `resetToIdle()`. `resetToIdle` must not delete a successful output file on disk.

Guard `start*` if already `Running`. Keep split start/wait only when the job must span a later UI step (`pendingConcatenator_` during game setup).

```cpp
// BAD — four-step sequence; getters are live object state
concatenator->startConcatenation(paths, dir);
if (!concatenator->waitWithProgress(this)) {
  warn(concatenator->errorMessage());
}

// GOOD — snapshot outlives resetToIdle
const VideoConcatenationResult result =
    concatenator.runWithProgress(paths, dir, this);
if (!result.succeeded) {
  warn(result.errorMessage);
}
```
